.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-mcp 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-mcp \- Dispatch a declared MCP call and hand back a reduction instead of the payload
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten mcp\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dispatch a declared MCP call and hand back a reduction instead of the payload
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-mcp\-call(1)
Dispatch one declared method, store the response, and print the declared reduction
.TP
batten\-mcp\-spawn(1)
Record that a client actually spawned this server, then exec the launch line unchanged
.TP
batten\-mcp\-grant(1)
Apply the committed MCP permissions to whichever server name the host exposed this session
.TP
batten\-mcp\-posture(1)
Refuse an enabled MCP server this session did not attach, or a grant the connector would still prompt for
.TP
batten\-mcp\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
